IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), PART III -- regulation 16: EMPLOYMENT OUTSIDE CANADA.
-- Piece cr1. LAYER 1.
--
-- Regulation 16(1) includes in pensionable employment employment outside Canada (other than in international
-- transportation) that would be pensionable if it were in Canada, for an employee who meets one of seven
-- descriptions (a) to (g). Regulation 16(2) includes employment in another country by an employer operating in
-- Canada, on three conditions and an undertaking. Paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act (piece cp1) and paragraphs
-- 250(1)(b) and (d) of the Income Tax Act (not deposited) are named by the text; whether a fact they decide holds
-- is a plain input here.
-- Whether the Treasury Board's President or a province "signifies" its wish is a plain input (a decision of
-- someone else, never guessed).

§ `Regulations, Part III -- regulation 16: employment outside Canada`

§§ `The facts about an employee employed outside Canada`

-- src:240 | 16 (1) Pensionable employment includes employment outside Canada (except employment in international transportation) that would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada, if the employee employed therein
-- src:241 | (a) ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of his employer;
-- src:242 | (b) is resident in Canada and is paid at or from an establishment in Canada of his employer;
-- src:243 | (c) is an employee, other than an employee engaged locally outside Canada,
-- src:244 | (i) of Her Majesty in right of Canada, or
-- src:245 | (ii) of Her Majesty in right of that province (if employment by Her Majesty in right of that province has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act),
-- src:246 | who was resident in Canada immediately prior to becoming so employed outside Canada or who is in receipt of a representation allowance;
-- src:247 | (d) performs services in a country other than Canada under an international development assistance program of the Government of Canada prescribed as such pursuant to paragraph 250(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act and was resident in Canada at any time in the three-month period preceding the day on which such services commenced;
-- src:248 | (e) is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in paragraph (c) or (d) or of a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act and
-- src:249 | (i) is living with that person,
-- src:250 | (ii) is an employee of Her Majesty in right of Canada or of Her Majesty in right of a province (the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act), and
-- src:251 | (iii) was resident in Canada at any time before becoming so employed outside Canada;
-- src:252 | (f) is an employee of Her Majesty in right of Canada who is engaged locally outside Canada and if the President of the Treasury Board signifies to the Minister that he wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment; or
-- src:253 | (g) is an employee of Her Majesty in right of a province (the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act), who is engaged locally outside Canada and if the government of the province signifies to the Minister that it wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment.
@ref Reg 16(1) (src:240-253)
DECLARE `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada` HAS
    `ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `engaged outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `engaged for the performance of services outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident in Canada immediately prior to becoming so employed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in receipt of a representation allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `performs services in a country other than Canada under an international development assistance program of the Government of Canada prescribed as such pursuant to paragraph 250(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident in Canada at any time in the three-month period preceding the day on which such services commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `living with the spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident in Canada at any time before becoming so employed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the President of the Treasury Board signifies to the Minister that he wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the government of the province signifies to the Minister that it wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Regulation 16(3) and the seven paragraphs of 16(1)`

-- 16 (3) In this section, the expression an employee engaged locally outside Canada means an employee who is
-- engaged outside Canada for the performance of services outside Canada.
-- src:260 | (3) In this section, the expression an employee engaged locally outside Canada means an employee who is engaged outside Canada for the performance of services outside Canada.
@ref Reg 16(3) (src:260)
GIVEN employee IS A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(3) — an employee is an employee engaged locally outside Canada` employee MEANS
    (employee's `engaged outside Canada`) AND (employee's `engaged for the performance of services outside Canada`)

-- src:241 | (a) ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of his employer;
@ref Reg 16(1)(a) (src:241)
GIVEN employee IS A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(1)(a) — the employee ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of the employer` employee MEANS
    employee's `ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of the employer`

-- src:242 | (b) is resident in Canada and is paid at or from an establishment in Canada of his employer;
@ref Reg 16(1)(b) (src:242)
GIVEN employee IS A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(1)(b) — the employee is resident in Canada and paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer` employee MEANS
    (employee's `resident in Canada`) AND (employee's `paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer`)

-- (c) an employee, other than an employee engaged locally outside Canada, of Her Majesty in right of Canada or
-- of Her Majesty in right of a province (if that employment has been included by regulation under 7(1)(e)) who
-- was resident in Canada immediately prior to becoming so employed outside Canada or who is in receipt of a
-- representation allowance.
-- src:243 | (c) is an employee, other than an employee engaged locally outside Canada,
-- src:244 | (i) of Her Majesty in right of Canada, or
-- src:245 | (ii) of Her Majesty in right of that province (if employment by Her Majesty in right of that province has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act),
-- src:246 | who was resident in Canada immediately prior to becoming so employed outside Canada or who is in receipt of a representation allowance;
@ref Reg 16(1)(c) (src:243-246)
GIVEN employee IS A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` employee MEANS
        (    (employee's `employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada`)
         OR  (employee's `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province whose employment has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act`))
    AND (NOT (`reg 16(3) — an employee is an employee engaged locally outside Canada` employee))
    AND (    (employee's `resident in Canada immediately prior to becoming so employed outside Canada`)
         OR  (employee's `in receipt of a representation allowance`))

-- src:247 | (d) performs services in a country other than Canada under an international development assistance program of the Government of Canada prescribed as such pursuant to paragraph 250(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act and was resident in Canada at any time in the three-month period preceding the day on which such services commenced;
@ref Reg 16(1)(d) (src:247)
GIVEN employee IS A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(1)(d) — the employee performs services under an international development assistance program` employee MEANS
        (employee's `performs services in a country other than Canada under an international development assistance program of the Government of Canada prescribed as such pursuant to paragraph 250(1)(d) of the Income Tax Act`)
    AND (employee's `resident in Canada at any time in the three-month period preceding the day on which such services commenced`)

-- (e) the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in paragraph (c) or (d) or of a person described
-- in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act, who (i) is living with that person, (ii) is an employee of Her
-- Majesty in right of Canada or of a province (the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to
-- in 7(1)(e)), and (iii) was resident in Canada at any time before becoming so employed outside Canada.
-- The other person is NOTHING when the employee is nobody's spouse or common-law partner.
-- src:248 | (e) is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in paragraph (c) or (d) or of a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act and
-- src:249 | (i) is living with that person,
-- src:250 | (ii) is an employee of Her Majesty in right of Canada or of Her Majesty in right of a province (the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act), and
-- src:251 | (iii) was resident in Canada at any time before becoming so employed outside Canada;
@ref Reg 16(1)(e) (src:248-251)
GIVEN employee IS A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
      partner IS A MAYBE `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` employee partner MEANS
    CONSIDER partner
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST other THEN
            (    (`reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` other)
             OR  (`reg 16(1)(d) — the employee performs services under an international development assistance program` other)
             OR  (other's `a person described in paragraph 250(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act`))
        AND (employee's `living with the spouse or common-law partner`)
        AND (    (employee's `employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada`)
             OR  (employee's `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act`))
        AND (employee's `resident in Canada at any time before becoming so employed outside Canada`)

-- (f) an employee of Her Majesty in right of Canada who is engaged locally outside Canada, if the President of
-- the Treasury Board signifies to the Minister that he wishes the employment included. (g) the same for an
-- employee of Her Majesty in right of a province whose government has entered into an agreement referred to in
-- 7(1)(e), if the government of the province signifies its wish.
-- src:252 | (f) is an employee of Her Majesty in right of Canada who is engaged locally outside Canada and if the President of the Treasury Board signifies to the Minister that he wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment; or
@ref Reg 16(1)(f) (src:252)
GIVEN employee IS A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(1)(f) — the Crown employee engaged locally is one the President of the Treasury Board wishes included` employee MEANS
        (employee's `employed by Her Majesty in right of Canada`)
    AND (`reg 16(3) — an employee is an employee engaged locally outside Canada` employee)
    AND (employee's `the President of the Treasury Board signifies to the Minister that he wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment`)

-- src:253 | (g) is an employee of Her Majesty in right of a province (the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act), who is engaged locally outside Canada and if the government of the province signifies to the Minister that it wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment.
@ref Reg 16(1)(g) (src:253)
GIVEN employee IS A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(1)(g) — the provincial employee engaged locally is one the province wishes included` employee MEANS
        (employee's `employed by Her Majesty in right of a province the government of which has entered into an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act`)
    AND (`reg 16(3) — an employee is an employee engaged locally outside Canada` employee)
    AND (employee's `the government of the province signifies to the Minister that it wishes the employment of such employee to be included in pensionable employment`)

§§ `Regulation 16(1) and 16(2)`

-- 16 (1) Pensionable employment includes employment outside Canada (except employment in international
-- transportation) that would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada, if the employee employed therein
-- meets one of paragraphs (a) to (g).
-- src:240 | 16 (1) Pensionable employment includes employment outside Canada (except employment in international transportation) that would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada, if the employee employed therein
@ref Reg 16(1) (src:240)
GIVEN `the employment is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is employment in international transportation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      employee IS A `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
      partner IS A MAYBE `cr1 Employee employed outside Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment outside Canada` `the employment is outside Canada` `the employment is employment in international transportation` `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada` employee partner MEANS
        `the employment is outside Canada`
    AND (NOT `the employment is employment in international transportation`)
    AND `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada`
    AND (    (`reg 16(1)(a) — the employee ordinarily reports for work at an establishment in Canada of the employer` employee)
         OR  (`reg 16(1)(b) — the employee is resident in Canada and paid at or from an establishment in Canada of the employer` employee)
         OR  (`reg 16(1)(c) — the employee is a Crown employee not engaged locally who was resident in Canada or receives a representation allowance` employee)
         OR  (`reg 16(1)(d) — the employee performs services under an international development assistance program` employee)
         OR  (`reg 16(1)(e) — the employee is the spouse or common-law partner of a person described in (c), (d) or 250(1)(b)` employee partner)
         OR  (`reg 16(1)(f) — the Crown employee engaged locally is one the President of the Treasury Board wishes included` employee)
         OR  (`reg 16(1)(g) — the provincial employee engaged locally is one the province wishes included` employee))

-- src:258 | (ii) was engaged by the employer not more than three months after the employee ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in paragraph (1)(c), (d) or (e),
@ref Reg 16(2)(b)(ii) (src:258)
GIVEN `the day the employee ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in paragraph (1)(c), (d) or (e)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the employer engaged the employee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(2)(b)(ii) — the employee was engaged not more than three months after ceasing to be employed outside Canada` `the day the employee ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in paragraph (1)(c), (d) or (e)` `the day the employer engaged the employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the employee ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in paragraph (1)(c), (d) or (e)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN `a date is within a time limit after a start date` `the day the employer engaged the employee` ceased (`a number of months` WITH `number of months` IS 3)

-- 16 (2) Pensionable employment includes employment in a country other than Canada (except employment
-- described in subsection (1) or employment in international transportation) by an employer operating in
-- Canada if (a) the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada, and (b) the employee (i)
-- was engaged by the employer when the employee was in and resident in Canada, or (ii) was engaged by the
-- employer not more than three months after the employee ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of
-- the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in 16(1)(c), (d) or (e), and the employer has undertaken
-- in prescribed form to make payment of the employee's and the employer's contributions in accordance with
-- section 8 in respect of all such employees (fork F11: the undertaking is a condition of every case).
-- src:254 | (2) Pensionable employment includes employment in a country other than Canada (except employment described in subsection (1) or employment in international transportation) by an employer operating in Canada if
-- src:255 | (a) the employment in that country would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada, and
-- src:256 | (b) the employee
-- src:257 | (i) was engaged by the employer at the time when the employee was in and was resident in Canada, or
-- src:258 | (ii) was engaged by the employer not more than three months after the employee ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in paragraph (1)(c), (d) or (e),
-- src:259 | and the employer has undertaken in prescribed form to make payment of the employee’s contributions and the employer’s contributions in accordance with section 8 in respect of all such employees employed by him in such employment in that country.
@ref Reg 16(2) (src:254-259)
GIVEN `the employment is in a country other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is described in subsection (1) or is employment in international transportation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is an employer operating in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee was engaged by the employer when in and resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the employee ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in paragraph (1)(c), (d) or (e)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the employer engaged the employee` IS A DATE
      `the employer has undertaken to make payment of the contributions in accordance with section 8 in respect of all such employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is in a form the Minister has authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment in another country` `the employment is in a country other than Canada` `the employment is described in subsection (1) or is employment in international transportation` `the employer is an employer operating in Canada` `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada` `the employee was engaged by the employer when in and resident in Canada` `the day the employee ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in paragraph (1)(c), (d) or (e)` `the day the employer engaged the employee` `the employer has undertaken to make payment of the contributions in accordance with section 8 in respect of all such employees` `the undertaking is in a form the Minister has authorized` MEANS
        `the employment is in a country other than Canada`
    AND (NOT `the employment is described in subsection (1) or is employment in international transportation`)
    AND `the employer is an employer operating in Canada`
    AND `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were in Canada`
    AND (    `the employee was engaged by the employer when in and resident in Canada`
         OR  `reg 16(2)(b)(ii) — the employee was engaged not more than three months after ceasing to be employed outside Canada` `the day the employee ceased to be employed outside Canada as a member of the Canadian Forces or in the circumstances described in paragraph (1)(c), (d) or (e)` `the day the employer engaged the employee`)
    AND `the employer has undertaken to make payment of the contributions in accordance with section 8 in respect of all such employees`
    AND (`s 2(1) — prescribed` `a form or the information to be given on a form` `the undertaking is in a form the Minister has authorized` FALSE FALSE)
